# Executor-Py SDK — DNA (Design Nucleotide)

## 1. Canonical Position

`hace/sdk/executor-py` provides Python-native **Fractal Executor** primitives
that mirror the Rust `hace-sdk-executor-cep` IPO contract:

```text
                     CONA (Fractal Executor)
                         │
                ┌────────┴────────┐
                ▼                 ▼
            CAPOR             RACOR
          (WHAT)            (HOW/WHERE)
                │                 │
                └────────┬────────┘
                         ▼
                    IPO Pipeline
                   (Input→Port→Execute→Gate→Output)
                         │
                         ▼
              Executor-Py / Executor-Rs (Native)
```

## 2. Architecture

```text
hace/sdk/executor-py/
├── .know/
│   ├── rc/dna.ail                 # THIS FILE — DNA (design nucleotide)
│   └── concept/architecture.ail   # Concept layer
├── src/
│   └── executor_py/
│       ├── __init__.py            # Public API exports
│       ├── core.py                # Core types (ExecuteParticle, ExecInput, ExecOutput, etc.)
│       ├── ipo.py                 # IPO Feature abstract trait (mirrors Rust IpoFeature)
│       ├── capor.py               # CaporRouter (capacity resolution — WHAT)
│       ├── racor.py               # RacRouter (route resolution — HOW/WHERE)
│       ├── evidence.py            # SepiProof + FEH/ALR sealing
│       ├── fan.py                 # FanId + FanCapability (FAN → capability)
│       ├── payload.py             # Nep / uni-payload types
│       ├── adapter.py             # LION/RION adapter interface
│       └── simple.py              # Default IPO orchestrator implementation
├── tests/
│   ├── test_core.py
│   ├── test_ipo.py
│   ├── test_capor.py
│   └── test_racor.py
└── pyproject.toml
```

## 3. Core Traits (Python)

### ExecuteParticle (mirrors Rust `ExecuteParticle`)

```python
class ExecuteParticle(ABC, Generic[T_in, T_out]):
    @abstractmethod
    async def execute(self, input: T_in, ctx: ExecContext) -> T_out:
        ...
```

### IpoFeature (mirrors Rust `IpoFeature`)

```python
class IpoFeature(ABC, Generic[Request, Response]):
    @abstractmethod
    async def input(self, request: Request) -> IpoInput: ...
    @abstractmethod
    def process(self, ipo_input: IpoInput) -> IpoProcess: ...
    @abstractmethod
    async def output(self, ipo_process: IpoProcess) -> Response: ...
    async def execute(self, request: Request) -> Response:  # default orchestration
        ...
```

## 4. Integration with py-text-editor

`py-text-editor` provides concrete `ExecuteParticle` implementations for:

| Capability | Python Executor Package | File |
|---|---|---|
| `io.mcp.server.core.file.*` | `text-editor/io/mcp/server/core/file.py` | 7 actions |
| `io.mcp.server.core.uri.*` | `text-editor/io/mcp/server/core/uri.py` | 6 actions |
| `io.mcp.server.core.str.*` | `text-editor/io/mcp/server/core/str.py` | 17 actions |
| `io.rac.cri.fdi.*` | `text-editor/io/rac/cri/fdi.py` | 29 FDI bindings |

Each registers as a `FanCapability` under `FanId`:

```yaml
fan_registrations:
  - id: "text-editor-io-mcp-server-core-file"
    capabilities: ["file.create_file", "file.read_file", "file.append_file", ...]
    executor: "py-text-editor"
    transport: "FDI"

  - id: "text-editor-io-mcp-server-core-str"
    capabilities: ["str.snake", "str.camel", "str.headline", ...]
    executor: "py-text-editor"
    transport: "FDI"

  - id: "text-editor-io-rac-cri-fdi"
    capabilities: ["fdi.file.create_file", "fdi.file.read_file", ...]
    executor: "py-text-editor"
    transport: "FDI"
```

## 5. IPO Orchestration (Python → LION/RION)

```text
IpoOrchestrator
    │
    ├── CaporRouter.resolve()     → CaporDecision (WHAT capacity)
    ├── RacRouter.resolve_route() → RoutePlan (HOW/WHERE transport)
    │
    ├── if transport ∈ {FDI, FFI}:
    │       → LION Machine (local native)
    ├── elif transport ∈ {HTTP, gRPC}:
    │       → RION Machine (remote IO)
    └── elif method == "stream":
            → SIO Stream (hace-sio-stream)
```

## 6. Canonical Contract Alignment

| Rust (executor-cep) | Python (executor-py) | Status |
|---|---|---|
| `IpoFeature` trait | `executor_py.IpoFeature` | ✓ Mirror |
| `IpoInput` struct | `executor_py.IpoInput` | ✓ Mirror |
| `IpoProcess` struct | `executor_py.IpoProcess` | ✓ Mirror |
| `IpoOutput` struct | `executor_py.IpoOutput` | ✓ Mirror |
| `IpoOrchestrator` | `executor_py.simple.DefaultIpoOrchestrator` | ✓ Mirror |
| `CaporRouter` trait | `executor_py.CaporRouter` | ✓ Mirror |
| `RacRouter` trait | `executor_py.RacRouter` | ✓ Mirror |
| `ExecuteParticle` trait | `executor_py.ExecuteParticle` | ✓ Mirror |
| `ExecContext` struct | `executor_py.ExecContext` | ✓ Mirror |
| `ExecInput` / `ExecOutput` | `executor_py.ExecInput` / `ExecOutput` | ✓ Mirror |
| `SepiProof` | `executor_py.SepiProof` | ✓ Mirror |
| `FanId` / `FanCapability` | `executor_py.FanId` / `FanCapability` | ✓ Mirror |
| `Nep` | `executor_py.Nep` | ✓ Mirror |
| `RacUri` | `executor_py.RacUri` | ✓ Mirror (re-export) |
| `RacRoute` | `executor_py.RacRoute` | ✓ Mirror |
| `ExecutionMode` | `executor_py.ExecutionMode` | ✓ Mirror |

## 7. DNA Invariants

```yaml
dna_invariants:
  - "executor-py mirrors executor-cep IPO contract exactly (1:1 trait mapping)"
  - "executor-py is for Python-native particles; NOT for wrapping Rust"
  - "executor-py delegates transport resolution to LION Machine (local) or RION Machine (remote)"
  - "Every execute() MUST produce SepiProof evidence (FEH + ALR)"
  - "Capor resolves WHAT; Racor resolves HOW/WHERE; never merged"
  - "py-text-editor capabilities register as FanCapability in executor-py FanRegistry"
```
